  {
    "id": "295d50cfc193ff3d",
    "type": "comment",
    "z": "6d021e54d551838e",
    "name": "Subflow description",
    "info": "# Insert Queue\n\nProcess of this subflow:\n 1. queue messages\n 2. insert message by message into postgresql node\n 3. drop the message from the queue, when it was processed succesfull\n 4. peek a new message from the queue\n 5. repeat\n\nEach input will be queued inside the q-gate node. (FIFO)\nDuring start of the subflow a Trigger will be activated. This trigger will send a \"control: peek\" message at a given interval.\nThis is necessary because when the queue is empty we need to periodically check if a new message is available.\nWhen a message is dequeued the trigger will be deactivated (msg.reset: true) until the message is processed by the postgresql node.\n",
    "x": 150,
    "y": 40,
    "wires": []
  },
  {
    "id": "34c4a2e5385414c4",
